content.explanation:
When the visual nodes are not enough, the **Code Node** lets you write custom JavaScript (or Python) to process data however you want.

**When to Use the Code Node:**
- Complex data transformations that expressions cannot handle
- Custom calculations (discounts, scoring, tax)
- Filtering items based on complex conditions
- Parsing non-standard data formats
- Generating dynamic data

**How It Works:**
The Code Node receives input items, runs your code, and returns output items.

**Basic Structure:**
```javascript
// Access all input items
const items = $input.all();

// Process each item
const results = items.map(item => {
  return {
    json: {
      name: item.json.name,
      processed: true
    }
  };
});

// Return processed items
return results;
```

**Key Variables Available:**
- `$input.all()` — All input items as an array
- `$input.first()` — The first input item
- `$input.item` — Current item (in 'Run Once for Each Item' mode)
- `$('Node Name').all()` — All items from a specific node
- `$now` — Current date/time
- `$execution.id` — Current execution ID

challenge.starterCode:
// Input: array of customer objects with name, email, total_spend
const items = $input.all();

// Your code here: filter and transform

return results;

challenge.solution:
const items = $input.all();

const results = items
  .filter(item => item.json.total_spend > 5000)
  .map(item => ({
    json: {
      name: item.json.name,
      total_spend: item.json.total_spend
    }
  }));

return results;

challenge.starterCode:
const items = $input.all();

// Each item has: { product, price, quantity }
// Add: discount (%) and final_price

return results;

challenge.solution:
const items = $input.all();

const results = items.map(item => {
  const { product, price, quantity } = item.json;

  let discount = 0;
  if (quantity >= 100) discount = 20;
  else if (quantity >= 50) discount = 10;
  else if (quantity >= 10) discount = 5;

  const final_price = price * quantity * (1 - discount / 100);

  return {
    json: {
      product,
      price,
      quantity,
      discount: discount + '%',
      final_price: Math.round(final_price * 100) / 100
    }
  };
});

return results;

challenge.starterCode:
const items = $input.all();

// Each item has: { product, price_usd }
// Add: price_inr and price_eur

return results;

challenge.solution:
const items = $input.all();

const USD_TO_INR = 83.5;
const USD_TO_EUR = 0.92;

const results = items.map(item => {
  const priceUsd = item.json.price_usd;
  return {
    json: {
      ...item.json,
      price_inr: Math.round(priceUsd * USD_TO_INR * 100) / 100,
      price_eur: Math.round(priceUsd * USD_TO_EUR * 100) / 100
    }
  };
});

return results;

